--------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Purpose & Architecture
--------------------------------------------------------------------

NoteSpaceLLM is an unprivileged, local-first PySide6 desktop application
and offline research companion designed as a private alternative to Google
NotebookLM. It enables document analysis, multi-document synthesis, RAG-assisted
inquiries, and structured report generation across PDF, Word (DOCX), Markdown,
plain text, spreadsheets (XLSX), and email archives (EML, MSG). A lightweight
Web/PWA Companion provides zero-server mobile review of exported workspaces.

The software is engineered with the following explicit invariants:
  * Local-First Privacy Boundary (INV-LOCAL-01): Documents, extracted texts,
    ChromaDB vector stores, and SQLite workspace indexes remain strictly on the
    local machine and are never transmitted to external cloud systems without
    explicit user configuration.
  * Unprivileged User-Space Execution (INV-LOCAL-02): RunAsInvoker non-elevation;
    both PySide6 desktop GUI and CLI run with regular user privileges without
    requiring administrator or elevated operating system rights.
  * Zero Unsolicited Egress (INV-LOCAL-03): Core document parsing, text chunking,
    and local vector retrieval perform zero unsolicited network calls; optional
    cloud LLM integrations (OpenAI, Anthropic) activate only upon explicit user
    selection and key provisioning.
  * Offline-First Local Model Execution (INV-LOCAL-04): Native integration with
    local Ollama instances provides private LLM synthesis without requiring an
    active internet connection.
  * Hardened Parser Security (INV-LOCAL-05): Dependency floors for document
    parsers (openpyxl>=3.1.3, PyMuPDF>=1.24.10, python-docx>=1.1.0) guard
    against XML entity expansion (CVE-2024-34064) and archive bombs.
  * Portable Workspace Serialization (INV-LOCAL-06): Standardized JSON workspace
    format (`notespacellm-workspace-v1.json`) allows safe, schema-validated
    interchange with external tools and mobile review companions.
  * PWA Offline Isolation (INV-LOCAL-07): The Web Companion operates 100%
    client-side via Service Worker caching with zero telemetry or tracking.
  * AGPL-3.0 & LGPL-3.0 Boundary Purity (INV-LOCAL-08): Full compliance with
    PyMuPDF AGPL-3.0 copyleft and PySide6 LGPL-3.0 dynamic linking isolation.
  * Version Freeze Discipline (INV-LOCAL-09): Strict compliance with policy
    T-20260920-167562623; hygiene and marketing passes never modify the
    application version outside authorized release ceremonies.
  * Statutory Disclaimer & SLA (INV-LOCAL-10): Unpaid open-source software under
    §§ 516 ff. BGB with liability governed by § 521 BGB; vulnerability reports
    are subject to a 48-hour acknowledgment and 5-day triage SLA.

